WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:02.030
- Y'all spent some time
in quarantine recreating

00:00:02.030 --> 00:00:03.460
old movie posters, right?

00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:04.750
With your kids, can we look at a few?

00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:05.583
- Yeah.

00:00:05.583 --> 00:00:06.997
- [Kelly] Okay, cool.

00:00:06.997 --> 00:00:07.915
Here we go.

00:00:07.915 --> 00:00:10.060
- Okay, so this is the original
poster of Audrey Hepburn

00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:11.380
in "Breakfast at Tiffany's."

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:14.590
And I had this crazy idea that
we should duplicate famous

00:00:14.590 --> 00:00:16.390
movie stills or posters with my kids.

00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:19.014
I don't know why I thought of
that, but they liked the idea.

00:00:19.014 --> 00:00:20.430
Okay yeah, there she is.

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:23.910
Okay, so that's Matea and that's
one of our rescue kittens.

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:26.833
That one is called
Creamy, orange creamsicle.

00:00:28.610 --> 00:00:30.970
We've been rescuing
kittens during quarantine.

00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:33.160
So I was doing her hair
and makeup and she,

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:35.620
at a certain point was like,
mommy, this is not perfect.

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:37.100
I cannot do this, I'm sorry.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:38.830
I'm sorry, I cannot,

00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:40.150
this is the best I could do.

00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:42.970
I'm not a professional
hair and makeup artist.

00:00:42.970 --> 00:00:44.800
- Let's see the next one, this is so cool.

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:46.840
Okay, this is the original, James Dean.

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:48.860
- Yeah. There's the original James Dean

00:00:49.999 --> 00:00:51.923
in "Rebel Without a Cause."

00:00:51.923 --> 00:00:54.900
And there's my son, Johnny,
my 14 year old rebel with,

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:55.960
or without a class.

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:58.476
And we actually showed them the movie

00:00:58.476 --> 00:00:59.373
and Johnny really loved it.

00:01:00.296 --> 00:01:01.670
So we had the red jacket, we had,

00:01:01.670 --> 00:01:03.410
if you look at the, the actual poster,

00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:04.310
it's really hard to see there,

00:01:04.310 --> 00:01:06.490
but it does have a sort
of blue corrugated looking

00:01:06.490 --> 00:01:07.630
background in it.

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:09.570
And we had this storage
container on the property.

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:12.950
So Johnny stood in front
of it and looked dreamy.

00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:15.610
- I mean, your family is the
most gorgeous family ever.

00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:17.430
The fact that they can
pull these posters off,

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:19.100
I wouldn't even attempt it.

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:21.750
Okay, here' "Giant," great film,

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:23.510
- Johnny's actually the
one who's responsible

00:01:23.510 --> 00:01:25.020
for putting all the graphics on,

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:27.130
together with all the images that we took.

00:01:27.130 --> 00:01:28.800
And Johnny's also an
awesome baseball player.

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:30.150
I just wanted to say that.

00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:32.190
Holden, who's in "Giant," is also an

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:35.390
amazing baseball player and "Giant"

00:01:35.390 --> 00:01:37.010
is another James Dean classic.

00:01:37.010 --> 00:01:39.857
And it kind of fits with
Hodlie's sort of like,

00:01:39.857 --> 00:01:43.160
well, I like to call Holden
my, my burnt marshmallow.

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:45.350
He's like hard and crispy on the outside

00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:46.690
and soft and gooey on the inside.

00:01:46.690 --> 00:01:48.310
He's an amazing, wonderful boy.

00:01:48.310 --> 00:01:49.970
And they're all very artistic.

00:01:49.970 --> 00:01:51.210
They love painting, drawing,

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:53.130
photography, anything to
do with all this stuff.

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:54.350
- Oh, I love, I love it.

00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:56.540
And they all have their own
like individual personalities.

00:01:56.540 --> 00:01:58.330
It's so crazy, even they grew
up in the same household.

00:01:58.330 --> 00:02:00.344
It's it is so funny,
everybody's still so different.

00:02:00.344 --> 00:02:01.680
Let's see the next one.

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:02.750
Oh, I love this one.

00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:04.630
Dorothy, original.

00:02:04.630 --> 00:02:06.470
- That's Lutia, she's eight years old.

00:02:06.470 --> 00:02:08.900
She's holding another one
of our rescue kittens.

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:10.476
I think that's Hufflepuff.

00:02:10.476 --> 00:02:13.200
Yeah. We also have a black,

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:15.205
sort of a black and
tan, Brindle, Frenchie,

00:02:15.205 --> 00:02:18.770
which may or may have
looked more like Toto,

00:02:18.770 --> 00:02:21.058
but we decided to use the kittens,

00:02:21.058 --> 00:02:23.860
but I think they just all really loved

00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:25.353
the dress-up aspect to this.

